        },
        "text_iHTCfJ": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Growing up on St. Simons Island, Georgia, I was surrounded by the natural beauty of the sea and coastal living. As a child, I experimented with marsh mud masks and sea salt sprays, unknowingly planting the seeds of Earth Harbor long before it became a reality. Years later, as a published, award-winning researcher specializing in environmental health and toxicology, I traveled the world studying how toxins affect our health and the environment. My work focused on uncovering natural alternatives that could transform wellness while protecting the planet, laying the foundation for what Earth Harbor would become.<\/p>",
            "size": 100,
            "text_position": "center",
            "spacing_bottom": 12
          }
        }
      },
